on $290M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 77% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $44M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 7.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $10.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-10271812.62},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}